# Ticket #116 — bidirectionality verification log

AltCompare rows get an `(alt)` marker. Each new pin is verified BIDIRECTIONALLY:
PASS with the real code → deliberately break the load-bearing term → observe the
pin genuinely FAIL by name → restore → green.

Target files:
  - `src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.ts` — `CandidateRow.isAlternate` (interface) and
    `isAlternate: candidate.isAlternate` (`candidateRowsFor`)
  - `src/ui/AltCompare.tsx` — the `{row.isAlternate && <span …> (alt)</span>}` child

The two new pins:
  1. `chain-builder-adapter.test.ts` — "carries isAlternate from the RECIPE, not
     from the selection (#116)"
  2. `AltCompare.test.tsx` — "marks the ALTERNATE row, whichever row is current
     (#116)"

Run inside the worktree:
`npx vitest run src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.test.ts src/ui/AltCompare.test.tsx`
(105 its = 103 pre-existing + the 2 new). Repo-root `npm test` double-counts
worktree tests — the worktree-local run is the trunk-true view.

**Every mutant below was typechecked (`npx tsc -b`) before its test run, and every
one COMPILES CLEAN.** A mutant that fails to compile proves nothing about a
test's discriminating power, so compile-validity is part of each entry.

