## The mutant family this log exists for

The field is set ONE LINE BELOW `isCurrent: candidate.id === currentRecipeId`, so
the plausible implementer slip is a verbatim copy of that line. Both fixtures hold
two candidates of which exactly one is an alternate, so `isAlternate` is a
**bijection** with `isCurrent` *whichever* recipe is current — a single-polarity
assertion cannot tell the two apart. Both pins therefore assert at BOTH polarities,
with the SAME expected value; that the expectation is identical at both is the point.

Break commands are applied by `mutate.py` (scratchpad harness, exact-anchor
replacement; refuses on anything but a unique match), then reverted with
`git checkout -- src/ui/chain-builder-adapter.ts src/ui/AltCompare.tsx`.

