## Assertion strings — verified byte-accurate, not assumed

The spec's two exact-substring assertions were checked against real
`renderToStaticMarkup` output rather than trusted. The emitted cell is exactly:

    <td>Alternate<span class="alt-compare-mark"> (alt)</span></td>

No `<!-- -->` separator appears (static markup emits none, and the marker child is
an ELEMENT, not a second text node); JSX preserves the span's leading space. The
spec's strings matched the bytes on the first run — no correction was needed.

Both assertion-form traps hold as the spec states:
  - the absence half is scoped to `<td>Standard</td>`; a bare
    `not.toContain("(alt)")` would be meaningless, since SSR returns ONE flat
    string containing both rows;
  - the presence half keeps the parens — the fixture's alternate is NAMED
    "Alternate", so a bare `"alt"` matches the recipe name alone.

## Deliberately not pinned (per spec)

The positional mutant (`isAlternate: index > 0`): neither map callback exposes an
index (`chain-builder-adapter.ts:950`, `AltCompare.tsx:149`), so reaching one
requires deliberately adding a parameter — not an implementer slip. Also unpinned:
the styling (the browser walk is this file's stated visual gate).
